T("Reading","Reading: The canoe trip","Read a story and answer","🛶","",
 ["Read the story once for what happens and once for how it feels.", "An author often shows feelings through actions, like holding your breath.", "A comparison such as \"as flat as glass\" paints a picture."],
 ["When did Grandpa and Noor set out?|Before sunrise|At noon|After supper|At midnight", "What does \"as flat as glass\" tell you about the water?|It was very calm|It was frozen|It was dirty|It was shallow", "Why did Grandpa tell Noor to paddle softly?|So they would not scare the animals|Because he was tired|Because the canoe was leaking|So they could go faster", "What was the moose doing?|Eating among the lilies|Swimming across the lake|Sleeping on the shore|Running through the trees", "Why did Noor hold her breath?|She was amazed and did not want to disturb the moose|She was under water|She was cold|She was angry", "How did the moose leave?|It walked calmly into the trees|It ran away in fear|It swam across the lake|It charged at the canoe", "What is the main feeling of this story?|Quiet wonder|Fear|Boredom|Anger"],"","Grandpa and Noor paddled across the lake before sunrise. The water was as flat as glass, and a loon called somewhere in the mist. \"Paddle softly,\" Grandpa whispered. Around the bend, a moose stood knee-deep in the lilies, eating its breakfast. Noor held her breath. For a whole minute nobody moved. Then the moose lifted its head, looked at them, and walked calmly into the trees. Noor knew she would remember that minute for the rest of her life.");
T("Reading","Reading: Maple syrup","Read facts and answer","🍁","",
 ["Look for numbers and what they measure.", "The word because tells you a reason is coming.", "Decide what the whole text is mostly about."],
 ["What does maple syrup begin as?|Sap|Sugar cane|Honey|Leaves", "When does the sap start to flow?|In early spring|In mid-summer|In late autumn|In the middle of winter", "About how much sap makes one litre of syrup?|About forty litres|About two litres|About ten litres|About one hundred litres", "Why is so much sap needed?|Most of the water is boiled away|Most of it is spilled|The trees drink it back|It freezes", "Which province makes most of Canada's maple syrup?|Quebec|Ontario|Alberta|Nova Scotia", "What weather makes the sap flow?|Freezing nights and warmer days|Hot days and hot nights|Heavy rain|Strong wind", "What is this text mostly about?|How maple syrup is made|How to cook pancakes|Why trees lose their leaves|The history of Quebec"],"","Maple syrup begins as sap inside sugar maple trees. In early spring, when nights are below freezing and days are warmer, the sap starts to flow. Farmers drill a small hole in the trunk and collect the watery sap. It takes about forty litres of sap to make just one litre of syrup, because most of the water must be boiled away. Canada makes most of the world's maple syrup, and most of that comes from Quebec.");
T("Spelling","Harder spellings","Believe, beautiful, Wednesday …","🔡","Which word is spelled correctly?",
 ["Some words have letters you cannot hear, like the d in Wednesday.", "A saying can help: there is \"a lie\" in believe.", "Read each choice slowly, part by part."],
 ["|believe|beleive|belive|beleve", "|beautiful|beutiful|beautifull|butiful", "|Wednesday|Wensday|Wednsday|Wendesday", "|February|Febuary|Februery|Feburary", "|surprise|suprise|surprize|serprise", "|minute|minit|minuite|minnute", "|favourite|favrite|faverite|favourit", "|neighbour|nieghbour|naybour|neighbur", "|necessary|neccessary|necesary|nessesary", "|separate|seperate|separete|sepparate"],"");
T("Words","Sayings (idioms)","Phrases that mean something else","💬","What does this saying mean?",
 ["An idiom is a saying that does not mean what the words say.", "\"It is raining cats and dogs\" just means it is raining very hard.", "Think about when people use the saying."],
 ["It is a piece of cake.|It is very easy.|It is very tasty.|It is very small.|It is broken.", "It is raining cats and dogs.|It is raining very hard.|Animals are falling.|It is a sunny day.|The pets are outside.", "I am feeling under the weather.|I feel a little sick.|I am standing in the rain.|I feel very happy.|I am cold.", "Time to hit the books.|Time to study.|Time to throw books.|Time to tidy up.|Time to go to bed.", "She let the cat out of the bag.|She told a secret.|She lost her cat.|She opened her bag.|She bought a pet.", "That costs an arm and a leg.|It is very expensive.|It is very painful.|It is very cheap.|It is the wrong size.", "It happens once in a blue moon.|It happens very rarely.|It happens every night.|It happens when it is cold.|It never happens.", "Break a leg!|Good luck!|Be careful!|Go away!|Sit down!", "He spilled the beans.|He told the secret.|He dropped his lunch.|He planted a garden.|He was clumsy.", "Hold your horses.|Wait a moment.|Ride faster.|Feed the animals.|Hold on tight."],"");

