T("Grammar","Prepositions","In, on, under, between and more","📍","Which word fits?",
 ["A preposition shows how one thing relates to another, often in place or time.", "Place: in the box, on the table, under the bed, between the trees.", "Time: at noon, on Monday, in July, before lunch, during the game."],
 ["The cat is hiding ___ the bed.|under|at|during|until", "We have music class ___ Tuesday.|on|in|at|by", "My birthday is ___ March.|in|on|at|to", "The game starts ___ seven o'clock.|at|in|on|of", "She sat ___ her two best friends.|between|among|into|above", "He walked ___ the bridge to the other side.|across|between|during|among", "Please wash your hands ___ dinner.|before|between|under|across", "Nobody talked ___ the test.|during|among|above|into", "The bird flew ___ the trees and out of sight.|over|at|on|until", "We divided the snacks ___ the five of us.|among|between|across|under", "The letter is ___ my aunt in Regina.|from|during|above|until"]);
T("Grammar","Complete sentences","Fragments and run-ons","🧩","",
 ["A complete sentence has a subject and a verb and gives a whole thought.", "A fragment is missing something: Ran down the hill.", "A run-on joins two sentences with no punctuation or joining word."],
 ["Which is a complete sentence?|The dog barked.|Barked at the door.|The big brown dog.|Because it was late.", "Which is a fragment?|After the game ended.|We went home.|The bell rang.|Snow fell all night.", "Which is a run-on sentence?|I like soup it is warm.|I like soup because it is warm.|I like soup. It is warm.|I like warm soup.", "What is missing from this fragment: Ran to the bus stop.|A subject|A verb|A period|A capital letter", "What is missing from this fragment: The tall girl in the red coat.|A verb|A subject|A noun|An adjective", "Which correctly fixes this run-on: We were late we ran.|We were late, so we ran.|We were late we, ran.|We were, late we ran.|We were late ran.", "Which is a complete sentence?|Maya laughed.|Laughing loudly.|When Maya laughed.|Maya and her friend.", "Which is a fragment?|Under the old bridge.|The river is deep.|Fish swim there.|We crossed it.", "Which correctly fixes this run-on: It rained the game was cancelled.|It rained. The game was cancelled.|It rained the game, was cancelled.|It, rained the game was cancelled.|It rained the game. Was cancelled.", "Which is a complete sentence?|Although it was cold, we played outside.|Although it was cold.|Playing outside in the cold.|The cold winter morning."]);
